# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AEGIS — every variable below is OPTIONAL.
# With no .env at all, AEGIS runs fully offline on in-memory storage with
# seeded demo data. Copy to `.env` only to enable an integration:
#     cp .env.example .env
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Claude-powered free-text triage on /api/triage. Without a key the same
# endpoint answers from a deterministic rules engine — same response shape,
# so the UI works identically either way.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Persistent storage (production only). Leave BOTH unset for local dev.
# Required when deploying to Vercel, where memory does not survive between
# serverless invocations. Add the Upstash integration from the Vercel
# Marketplace and these are injected automatically.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-database.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=your-token

# Extra origins the /api/ext reverse proxy may forward to (comma-separated),
# used when integrating modules acquired on the trading floor. Localhost
# module ports 4101/4102/4104 are always allowed.
# AEGIS_EXT_ALLOWLIST=https://seller-module.vercel.app

# Shared state for a deployed AEGIS. Serverless invocations share no memory,
# so without this a report filed by one instance is invisible to the next.
# Created with `vercel blob create-store <name> --access private --yes`, which
# also links it to the project and sets this variable for you.
# Leave it unset locally: a fresh clone runs on the in-memory store with no
# configuration at all.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=vercel_blob_rw_...

# Real WhatsApp intake. Point your Twilio WhatsApp sandbox webhook at
# POST /api/intake/whatsapp, then set this to the auth token from the Twilio
# console so only genuinely signed requests are filed — the endpoint is public
# by necessity, and raising emergency incidents should not be open to anyone
# who finds the URL.
# Leave it unset to accept any request, which is what makes the browser-console
# demo work with no Twilio account.
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=your_twilio_auth_token
